<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pope Martin V</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1369">1369</a>–<a href="/years/1431">1431</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Oddone Colonna</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Martin V, born Oddone <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colonna-family">Colonna</a>, was pope from 1417 to 1431. His election at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-constance">Council of Constance</a> ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-schism">Western Schism</a>, during which rival popes had competed for nearly 40 years. He returned the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, restored its authority over the Papal States and resisted the conciliar movement's claims to authority over the pope.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-martin-v.jpg" alt="Pope Martin V" width="320" height="396" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Venetian school / After Pisanello · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Papa_Martino_V.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
